# fixedbugs, defect 151, lane land186, 2026-10-02 (panel 186 R1), the cost
# the panel's completeness critic found in the route.
#
# SYMPTOM, on the route as the sitting built it: a record the layout check must
# read, here because it holds an anonymous union, over defect 140's thousand
# structs nested by value. clang's record-layout dump prints one block per
# record it lays out and expands every named member inline, so it grows with
# the cube of the depth: 348,380,566 bytes for this program, all of it kept
# under `build/` and cut into rows, the compiler at 1,127,399,424 bytes
# resident (`/usr/bin/time -l`, a busy Mac, 2026-10-02).
#
# FIX: only the blocks this compiler asked for become rows and are kept
# (`emit/layout_rows.hero`); the rest is stepped over a byte at a time.
# Measured the same way the same day: 1,029,643 bytes kept, 719,388,672
# resident at the peak, which is clang's own output read once (the runtime's
# file read holds it twice) and released. The program reads the arm C wrote.

extern "fixedbugs-151-a-flagged-record-over-a-thousand-deep-nest-builds.h"
    record G0
        v: i64
    record G1
        inner: G0
